  "description": "Conformance test 10 (CanCreateLot, \u00a78.4). In real mode with current zone 0, CanCreateLot(x, z, w, h, zoneNotNeeded, waterAllowed, null) is the minimum cell code over the rect (0 outside, 1 water, 2 not zoned, 3 network, 7 occupied, 8 free). Each scenario uses a separate area of the map. With a lot and a road on the rect the minimum is 3; without the road 7; without either 8; an unzoned cell inside gives 2, and zoneNotNeeded = 1 skips that check (8); a water cell with waterAllowed = 0 gives 1; a rect reaching x = 64 (outside the city) gives 0.",
